  "term": "Bulimia Nervosa",
  "definition": "Bulimia nervosa is an eating disorder marked by repeated binge eating followed by behaviors intended to prevent weight gain. These compensatory behaviors can include self-induced vomiting, misuse of laxatives or diuretics, excessive exercise, or fasting.",
